<title>LITHUANIA: SECURITIES COMMISSION REGISTERS NEW ISSUES.</title>
<headline>SECURITIES COMMISSION REGISTERS NEW ISSUES.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lithuanian Securities</p>
<p>commission said on Tuesday that it had registered 11 share</p>
<p>issues last Friday.</p>
<p>The securities commission said the following companies had</p>
<p>increased their share capital from internal reserves. All</p>
<p>figures in litas:</p>
<p>			    Number of     Face value  Share capital</p>
<p>			    new shares		    after the boost</p>
<p>    1. Sema	     1,037,251     5	     20,695,565</p>
<p>    2. Sanitas	  167,984	 25	    17,279,625</p>
<p>3. Ortopedijos</p>
<p>	 technika	 572,872	 2	     11,235,488</p>
<p>    4. Statrema	 15,341	  28	    429,548</p>
<p>5. Informacinio</p>
<p>verslo paslaugu</p>
<p>    imone		 32,674	  59	    1,927,766</p>
<p>    6. Vilkma	   624,014	 1	     1,248,028</p>
<p>    7. IGLUS	    221,146	 10	    221,460</p>
<p>The Securities comission said the following companies</p>
<p>registered new share capital raised by external issues:</p>
<p>			 New share issue Face value   Share capital</p>
<p>								after the boost</p>
<p>    1. Hermis bank  23,000,000	50	    90,000,000</p>
<p>    2. Montuotojas  959,500	   1	     3,428,053</p>
<p>The securities commission on Friday registered 3.6 million</p>
<p>ordinary shares of Tauras Bank with a face value of 10 litas.</p>
<p>The bank is now a publicly listed company. The bourse will now</p>
<p>decide when its shares will be traded.</p>
<p>A total of 100,000 ordinary shares of investment company</p>
<p>Alna Res with a face value of 10 litas were also registered,</p>
<p>transforming it into a publicly listed company.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
